 34MG dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 21-Apr-2026)          
 34MG c  2013Do22: a 345-MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca primary beam was accelerated by the
 34MG2c  superconducting ring cyclotron (SRC) at RIKEN. Secondary beams of      
 34MG3c  39Al+40Si and 37Al+36Mg were produced by the fragmentation of {+48}Ca  
 34MG4c  on a Be target and separated by the BigRIPS separator using the        
 34MG5c  B|r-|DE-B|r method. The secondary reaction target was 2.54-g/cm{+2}    
 34MG6c  thick carbon. The secondary reaction products {+38}Mg and              
 34MG7c  {+34}Mg+{+36}Mg in another setting, were identified by the magnetic    
 34MG8c  spectrometer ZeroDegree using the B|r-|DE-ToF method. |g rays in       
 34MG9c  coincidence with {+34}Mg were detected using the DALI2 array of 186    
 34MGAc  large NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured E|g with Doppler correction, I|g,    
 34MGBc  ({+34}Mg)|g-coin, and |g|g-coin. Deduced levels. Compared with         
 34MGCc  shell-model calculations using the SPDF-M effective interaction.       
 34MG cG E$From 2013Do22.                                                       
 34MG cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies. The observed energies of
 34MG2cL the first 4+ level and the first 2+ level yield an R{-4/2}=3.14 {I5},  
 34MG3cL which demonstrates that {+34}Mg is strongly deformed (2013Do22).       
 34MG cL J$No direct evidence for definite spin assignments was obtained from   
 34MG2cL the experiment but J|p can be assigned based on systematics among      
 34MG3cL magnesium isotopes and shell-model predictions (2013Do22).             
